# Combined-dataset template: real photos (Kaggle) + this project's reviewed
# simulator frames (roboflow_dataset/), so training doesn't forget what the
# model already learned from real photos while adding the sim data - unlike
# training on sim data alone in a separate run, which was confirmed this
# session to wipe out real-photo detection entirely (see conversation:
# train-11 went from correctly calling a real photo "smoke 0.87" to no
# detection at all, after 100 epochs on sim-only data).
#
# IMPORTANT: models/fire_smoke.pt is currently the sim-only train-11 model
# (promoted to production because it performs much better in the actual
# Webots app - see conversation). It is NOT the right starting point for
# this run. The original real-photo-only checkpoint is preserved at
# models/fire_smoke_real_only.pt specifically for this - use that as
# --weights below, not models/fire_smoke.pt.
#
# Setup on the training machine:
#   1. Copy this repo's roboflow_dataset/ folder over if it isn't already on
#      this machine (it's gitignored - not in git history - so it has to be
#      copied by hand: zip it up, or copy the folder directly).
#   2. Download the real dataset from the Kaggle link in README.md if you
#      don't already have it locally on this machine.
#   3. Copy this file to combined_data.yaml and fill in the two <...>
#      placeholders below with real absolute paths on THIS machine
#      (ultralytics has been observed resolving a relative `path:`/train/val
#      against the current working directory rather than this file's own
#      directory, which silently breaks things if you run training from
#      anywhere other than this file's folder - use absolute paths).
#   4. IMPORTANT: check the real dataset's own data.yaml `names:` list
#      matches this order (0: fire, 1: smoke) before training - if it
#      doesn't, the classes will be silently swapped/corrupted during
#      training. roboflow_dataset/data.yaml already confirmed to use this
#      order; the real dataset hasn't been checked from this machine.
#
# Then, for an overnight run:
#   python train.py --data combined_data.yaml --weights models/fire_smoke_real_only.pt --epochs 100 --batch 16
#
# (--device auto-detects the GPU, no need to pass it.)

train:
  - <ABSOLUTE PATH TO REAL DATASET>/images/train
  - <ABSOLUTE PATH TO THIS REPO>/roboflow_dataset/train/images
val:
  - <ABSOLUTE PATH TO REAL DATASET>/images/val
  - <ABSOLUTE PATH TO THIS REPO>/roboflow_dataset/valid/images

nc: 2
names:
  0: fire
  1: smoke
